WEBVTT

00:00:04.380 --> 00:00:05.760
Captain Starlog supplemental.

00:00:06.750 --> 00:00:09.890
It's been almost four days since the incident in the Romulan minefield.

00:00:10.660 --> 00:00:12.580
The repair teams have been working around the clock.

00:00:13.440 --> 00:00:14.800
Nerves are definitely frayed.

00:00:15.300 --> 00:00:17.060
It's incredible we're still in one piece.

00:00:17.660 --> 00:00:19.680
That mine and hit another meter to the left.

00:00:21.020 --> 00:00:24.370
We can't polarize the port bow plating until those breaches are sealed.

00:00:26.780 --> 00:00:27.770
What's your guess?

00:00:28.610 --> 00:00:30.000
Assuming we can find some tritets?

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:40.980
And with this kind of damage, the best I can give you is warp two, maybe 2.1.

00:00:40.980 --> 00:00:49.490
In other words, we're a decade away from Jupiter Station.

00:00:49.490 --> 00:00:56.230
What about the transceiver array?

00:00:56.230 --> 00:01:00.000
The subspace antenna is damaged.

00:01:00.030 --> 00:01:07.700
short range we've answered enough calls for help over the past year it's time someone returned the

00:01:07.700 --> 00:01:22.560
favor you serious archer to ensign sato go ahead sir i want you to get started on a general distress

00:01:22.560 --> 00:01:29.410
call assistance required minor repairs don't go into too much detail understood sir

00:01:30.670 --> 00:01:58.270
I will see my dream come alive and last.

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:01.660
Touch the sky

00:02:01.660 --> 00:02:06.250
They're not gonna hold me down no more

00:02:06.250 --> 00:02:09.220
No, they're not gonna change my mind

00:02:09.220 --> 00:02:13.190
Cause I've got faith in the heart

00:03:02.840 --> 00:03:04.160
You're killing me!

00:03:05.580 --> 00:03:07.070
Push, Lieutenant.

00:03:07.070 --> 00:03:09.160
Two more seconds.

00:03:09.160 --> 00:03:10.630
And rest.

00:03:10.630 --> 00:03:11.620
Gah!

00:03:11.620 --> 00:03:13.400
Gah!

00:03:13.400 --> 00:03:17.260
It can't be ethical to cause a patient this much pain.

00:03:17.260 --> 00:03:21.370
It's unethical to harm a patient I can inflict as much pain as I like.

00:03:21.370 --> 00:03:25.060
Positive attitude is vital to the healing process.

00:03:25.060 --> 00:03:28.440
The more you complain, the longer your recovery is likely to take.

00:03:28.440 --> 00:03:29.730
Ah!

00:03:30.090 --> 00:03:32.490
- When will I be able to return to duty?

00:03:32.490 --> 00:03:34.370
- Another week, possibly two.

00:03:34.370 --> 00:03:35.570
- Two weeks?

00:03:35.570 --> 00:03:38.020
- Attitude, Lieutenant.

00:03:38.020 --> 00:03:39.620
The wound might heal faster if you'd allow me

00:03:39.620 --> 00:03:41.880
to apply a few more Regulin bloodworms.

00:03:41.880 --> 00:03:43.120
- You're not putting any more of those things

00:03:43.120 --> 00:03:44.750
inside my leg.

00:03:44.750 --> 00:03:46.550
You still haven't found the last one.

00:03:46.550 --> 00:03:49.330
- He'll come out on his own, surely.

00:03:55.650 --> 00:03:56.850
- Did you hear that?

00:04:00.350 --> 00:04:09.340
believe it. Trip told me he fixed that squeak. Go ahead. Captain, we're receiving a response

00:04:09.340 --> 00:04:23.220
to the distress call. It's a Tellarite freighter. Put them through. This is Captain Archer

00:04:23.220 --> 00:04:30.000
of the Starship Enterprise. Thank you for responding. We need a

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:34.470
in repairing some hull damage if you can rendezvous with us we'd be happy to

00:04:34.470 --> 00:04:52.480
discuss I'm sorry sir they're barely within range can you repeat sounded like

00:04:52.480 --> 00:04:57.370
he said repair station we've received a set of coordinates what do you know

00:04:57.370 --> 00:05:00.000
about these tellerites they're not the most agreeable speed

00:05:00.030 --> 00:05:02.030
But they're usually trustworthy.

00:05:02.030 --> 00:05:05.660
The coordinates are three and a half days away at warp two.

00:05:05.660 --> 00:05:11.190
I think it's worth a look.

00:05:11.190 --> 00:05:12.720
Aye, sir.

00:05:12.720 --> 00:05:23.120
This is Captain Archer of the Starship Enterprise.

00:05:23.120 --> 00:05:25.330
We need to make some repairs.

00:05:25.330 --> 00:05:27.330
I was told you might be willing to help us.

00:05:35.240 --> 00:05:37.860
We'd be grateful for any assistance you could offer.

00:05:38.580 --> 00:05:39.220
Please respond.

00:05:43.480 --> 00:05:46.460
Nothing.

00:05:47.750 --> 00:05:48.270
Bioscience?

00:05:49.320 --> 00:05:50.400
None that I can detect.

00:05:51.170 --> 00:05:52.010
Maybe it's abandoned.

00:05:52.930 --> 00:05:54.370
We might be able to board it.

00:05:55.640 --> 00:05:56.920
Salvage some of the materials we need.

00:05:57.970 --> 00:06:00.000
Doesn't seem that Enterprise could fit inside those dots.

00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:11.240
what's it look like inside I'm detecting a liquid helium atmosphere the

00:06:11.240 --> 00:06:24.680
temperatures 270 degrees below zero biomolecular probe sir

00:06:38.890 --> 00:06:45.120
it's reconfiguring to fit the saucer section the liquid helium is being

00:06:45.120 --> 00:06:48.380
replaced by a warmer oxygen nitrogen atmosphere

00:06:48.380 --> 00:06:55.320
still no response to our hails it appears an invitation's been extended

00:06:55.320 --> 00:06:57.810
they need to work a little on their hospitality

00:07:01.310 --> 00:07:03.270
I don't see that we have a lot of options.

00:07:03.270 --> 00:07:07.650
Take a simple.

00:08:30.060 --> 00:08:33.800
They've isolated every hull breach, every damaged system.

00:08:36.350 --> 00:08:36.910
I'll be damned.

00:08:39.390 --> 00:08:41.530
We scratched the hull right there a year ago.

00:08:42.610 --> 00:08:44.150
I bumped it with the inspection pod, remember?

00:08:44.930 --> 00:08:47.180
I thought I told you to have that repainted.

00:08:49.050 --> 00:08:50.000
I was getting around to it.

00:08:56.620 --> 00:09:00.000
Everything's in English.

00:09:09.440 --> 00:09:11.000
The ship wasn't the only thing they probed.

00:09:12.320 --> 00:09:13.590
I think that's Malcolm.

00:09:15.340 --> 00:09:16.770
That's where his left leg was injured.

00:09:20.040 --> 00:09:23.400
This facility may have the technology to repair Mr. Reed as well.

00:09:26.540 --> 00:09:28.540
The analysis of your vessel is complete.

00:09:29.270 --> 00:09:30.000
Select a method of...

00:09:30.350 --> 00:09:38.220
to begin the repair process who am I speaking with your inquiry was not

00:09:38.220 --> 00:09:45.200
recognized is there someone here I can speak with your inquiry was not

00:09:45.200 --> 00:09:51.320
recognized I don't think there's anyone back there perhaps the stations automated

00:09:51.320 --> 00:10:00.000
are you saying you can repair all our systems select a method of compensation to be

00:10:00.000 --> 00:10:09.830
We can give them either three warp coils, five deuterium injectors, or 200 liters of warp plasma.

00:10:09.830 --> 00:10:13.800
I wouldn't recommend giving up any hardware we can't replace.

00:10:13.800 --> 00:10:18.430
Plasma? I think we can spare it.

00:10:18.430 --> 00:10:24.460
If we agree to these terms, how long will the repairs take?

00:10:24.460 --> 00:10:29.410
Time to completion: 34.2 Earth hours.

00:10:31.920 --> 00:10:35.420
I'm telling you, the boys at Jupiter Station would take three months.

00:10:36.750 --> 00:10:37.750
It's a fair exchange.

00:10:39.150 --> 00:10:42.150
Select a method of compensation to begin the repair process.

00:10:56.040 --> 00:10:58.550
Compensation will be due when the repairs are completed.

00:10:58.870 --> 00:11:00.000
Your vessel will then disappear.

00:11:00.000 --> 00:11:05.600
Engage immediately. All personnel are required to vacate areas that are undergoing reconstruction.

00:11:05.600 --> 00:11:08.480
Look at this.

00:11:08.480 --> 00:11:11.260
It's the repair schedule.

00:11:11.260 --> 00:11:27.800
Transmit it to Hoshi and have her inform the crew.

00:11:27.800 --> 00:11:30.000
Go ahead.

00:11:30.000 --> 00:11:32.360
arms are being attached to the outer hull.

00:11:32.360 --> 00:11:34.480
It's alright, Travis. Stand by.

00:11:34.480 --> 00:11:42.000
The recreation facility is now available to all personnel. Enjoy your visit.

00:12:15.770 --> 00:12:19.100
- If this is their idea of a recreation facility,

00:12:19.100 --> 00:12:20.680
we might want to ask for our plasma back.

00:12:34.760 --> 00:12:38.850
- A matter energy converter.

00:12:38.850 --> 00:12:44.380
- It could be a transporter, an awfully small one.

00:12:44.380 --> 00:12:47.400
- I believe it's a molecular synthesizer of some kind,

00:12:47.400 --> 00:12:49.240
similar to a protein resequencer,

00:12:49.240 --> 00:12:51.640
but far more advanced to water, cold.

00:13:07.320 --> 00:13:09.980
I saw a similar device in a Tarkaelian vessel.

00:13:09.980 --> 00:13:13.570
It was capable of replicating almost any inanimate object.

00:13:13.570 --> 00:13:15.420
If we had one of these in engineering,

00:13:15.420 --> 00:13:18.570
we could make all the spare parts we need.

00:13:18.570 --> 00:13:24.590
I wonder what else is on the menu.

00:13:24.590 --> 00:13:26.210
One pan fried catfish.

00:13:39.690 --> 00:13:53.620
- Smells like the real thing.

00:13:53.620 --> 00:13:56.410
- There's a catfish within 130 light years.

00:13:56.410 --> 00:13:58.590
- Its genome is stored in Enterprise's computer,

00:13:58.590 --> 00:13:59.800
as is the recipe.

00:14:01.310 --> 00:14:03.310
The station evidently scanned our database.

00:14:07.400 --> 00:14:08.740
It would have been nice to have been asked.

00:14:10.780 --> 00:14:13.310
Can we imagine what else this thing knows about us?

00:14:13.900 --> 00:14:15.000
Captain, you gotta try this.

00:14:15.730 --> 00:14:17.710
Thanks, but I'll stick with whatever chef's serving.

00:14:19.300 --> 00:14:19.900
I'll be on the bridge.

00:14:43.180 --> 00:14:48.160
sure this thing knows what it's doing that's the third time you've asked you

00:14:48.160 --> 00:14:51.800
didn't answer me the first two times it's remarkable your cells are

00:14:51.800 --> 00:14:56.020
regenerating at an exponential rate you see I was using a cytokinetic enzyme to

00:14:56.020 --> 00:15:00.000
stimulate the cell division lovely it certainly is a device like this

00:15:02.110 --> 00:15:04.870
Captain could negotiate a trade of some sort.

00:15:04.870 --> 00:15:21.990
Issue is completely healed, and the scar is gone.

00:15:21.990 --> 00:15:23.270
Try standing up.

00:15:23.270 --> 00:15:29.030
Any pain?

00:15:30.640 --> 00:15:44.860
none come in repairs are currently underway on c deck work on launch bay one is scheduled to

00:15:44.860 --> 00:15:56.270
begin at 2200 hours they even fixed the squeak in the floor starting to wonder if we had a gremlin

00:15:56.270 --> 00:16:00.000
under the deck plating a mythical creed

00:16:00.000 --> 00:16:04.530
British pilots used to blame them for problems they couldn't explain.

00:16:04.530 --> 00:16:06.950
Perhaps I should scan for one.

00:16:06.950 --> 00:16:09.450
That won't be necessary.

00:16:09.450 --> 00:16:13.450
Is Tripp happy with how the repairs are going?

00:16:13.450 --> 00:16:16.180
He says they're exceeding Starfleet specifications.

00:16:16.180 --> 00:16:17.180
That's good to hear.

00:16:17.180 --> 00:16:19.480
Anything else?

00:16:19.480 --> 00:16:21.920
If I may make an observation.

00:16:21.920 --> 00:16:22.870
Go ahead.

00:16:22.870 --> 00:16:24.190
You seem troubled.

00:16:24.190 --> 00:16:29.320
Guess I need to do a better job at repressing my emotions.

00:16:31.660 --> 00:16:36.310
These repairs are one hell of a bargain at only 200 liters of warp plasma, don't you think?

00:16:36.310 --> 00:16:40.550
Not every culture is based on the acquisition of wealth.

00:16:40.550 --> 00:16:44.600
The station's builders could simply have been interested in helping others.

00:16:44.600 --> 00:16:47.400
What happened to them?

00:16:47.400 --> 00:16:49.420
They could have at least left a message.

00:16:49.420 --> 00:16:51.620
Thanks for stopping by.

00:16:51.620 --> 00:16:55.180
Perhaps they prefer anonymity.

00:16:55.180 --> 00:16:57.840
Don't you find that a little suspicious?

00:17:00.030 --> 00:17:06.260
I know you don't put a lot of faith in your feelings, but I've learned to trust mine.

00:17:10.120 --> 00:17:11.240
Something doesn't smell right.

00:17:23.900 --> 00:17:26.750
Sorry, there wasn't anything for him to do.

00:17:26.810 --> 00:17:28.730
Stand there and watch this thing work.

00:17:29.080 --> 00:17:30.000
I must have felt.

00:17:30.640 --> 00:17:39.150
saw an entire translator assembly replaced in 15 minutes it would have taken my crew a week with

00:17:39.150 --> 00:17:44.330
this kind of technology starfleet could build ships that maintain themselves they wouldn't need

00:17:44.330 --> 00:17:51.260
chief engineers or tactical officers a starship without a tactical officer i can't say i see the

00:17:51.260 --> 00:17:55.570
point you'd think a computer that can do all this would have to be pretty big

00:17:55.570 --> 00:18:00.000
our computer is the most advanced in the fleet and it's three decks high

00:18:01.340 --> 00:18:03.860
- Well, I suppose you're right.

00:18:03.860 --> 00:18:07.260
- So where is it?

00:18:07.260 --> 00:18:09.610
- I don't follow.

00:18:09.610 --> 00:18:13.410
- I ran a scan of the station a few hours ago.

00:18:13.410 --> 00:18:15.560
These are the docking berths.

00:18:15.560 --> 00:18:17.100
We're here.

00:18:17.100 --> 00:18:22.590
This is the diagnostic room.

00:18:22.590 --> 00:18:26.900
- Well, that compartment's the only place it could be.

00:18:26.900 --> 00:18:30.000
And it's barely half the size of this one.

00:18:30.000 --> 00:18:36.770
capable of billions of calculations every nanosecond and it can fit inside the proverbial

00:18:36.770 --> 00:18:46.120
breadbox I'd love to get a look at that and you could always ask I tried your

00:18:46.120 --> 00:18:56.670
inquiry was not recognized well I guess that's not not necessarily this cooling

00:18:56.670 --> 00:18:59.890
duct runs all the way to the center of the station

00:19:00.440 --> 00:19:03.430
I saw an access port in one of the corridors.

00:19:03.430 --> 00:19:08.730
This computer might not take kindly to people snooping around.

00:19:08.730 --> 00:19:13.520
I haven't seen any no trespassing signs.

00:19:13.520 --> 00:19:16.600
We're explorers.

00:19:16.600 --> 00:19:18.290
Where's your spirit of adventure?

00:19:18.290 --> 00:19:20.200
I left it in a Romulan minefield.

00:19:31.440 --> 00:19:33.440
Almost.

00:19:33.440 --> 00:19:35.750
Got it.

00:19:35.750 --> 00:19:40.560
If the captain learns about this, we'll both be scrubbing plasma conduits for a month.

00:20:05.920 --> 00:20:07.110
- Mayweather.

00:20:07.110 --> 00:20:08.630
- Travis, it's the captain.

00:20:08.630 --> 00:20:11.710
Do you mind coming down to launch bay one?

00:20:11.710 --> 00:20:13.820
- I thought that section was off limits, sir.

00:20:13.820 --> 00:20:15.060
- Not anymore.

00:20:15.060 --> 00:20:17.120
I could use a hand, Ensign.

00:20:17.120 --> 00:20:18.240
- Aye, sir.

00:20:30.510 --> 00:20:32.510
"Are you sure this is the right direction?"

00:20:40.310 --> 00:20:48.660
"What's up, Commander?"

00:20:48.660 --> 00:20:56.020
"Captain?"

00:21:01.630 --> 00:21:05.240
- Hello?

00:21:05.240 --> 00:21:23.130
- Hello?

00:21:23.130 --> 00:21:26.010
- You know how stupid that little stunt was?

00:21:26.010 --> 00:21:28.420
He'd just have easily been transported out into space.

00:21:30.440 --> 00:21:34.080
You're senior officers. You're supposed to be setting an example for the rest of the crew.

00:21:34.950 --> 00:21:35.950
It was my idea, sir.

00:21:37.080 --> 00:21:39.160
I think Lieutenant Reed is old enough to make his own decisions.

00:21:42.200 --> 00:21:45.680
You've made it clear to me that you think discipline aboard Enterprise has gotten a little too lax.

00:21:46.180 --> 00:21:47.990
I'm beginning to agree with you.

00:21:50.300 --> 00:21:53.000
You're both restricted to quarters until further notice. Dismissed.

00:21:53.820 --> 00:21:54.200
Aye, sir.

00:21:55.990 --> 00:21:56.600
Hold on.

00:22:00.890 --> 00:22:04.250
- Did you notice anything interesting

00:22:04.250 --> 00:22:05.830
when you were in there?

00:22:05.830 --> 00:22:10.160
- Depends on what you mean by interesting.

00:22:10.160 --> 00:22:14.490
- T'Pol to Captain Archer.

00:22:14.490 --> 00:22:15.350
- Go ahead.

00:22:15.350 --> 00:22:16.930
- Needed in launch bay one.

00:22:30.410 --> 00:22:40.050
- He's dead, Captain.

00:22:40.050 --> 00:22:42.050
- These subcutaneous burns are consistent

00:22:42.050 --> 00:22:44.890
with an isolytic shock, but I can't be certain

00:22:44.890 --> 00:22:50.380
until I perform a full post-mortem.

00:22:50.380 --> 00:22:51.440
I'll keep you apprised.

00:23:01.790 --> 00:23:04.790
Looks like he was trying to tap into the EPS grid when this relay overloaded.

00:23:04.790 --> 00:23:10.950
Why the hell would he come down here during his off hours and start tampering with the power systems?

00:23:10.950 --> 00:23:15.520
I don't get it. Travis would have checked with me before doing any maintenance.

00:23:15.520 --> 00:23:18.520
Did you notify the crew that this section was off limits?

00:23:18.520 --> 00:23:19.500
Yes.

00:23:19.500 --> 00:23:23.760
Well, apparently somebody didn't get the message.

00:23:23.760 --> 00:23:25.360
What time did he go off duty?

00:23:25.360 --> 00:23:26.220
1,800 hours.

00:23:26.220 --> 00:23:29.240
Malcolm and I saw him in the station about a half an hour later.

00:23:29.240 --> 00:23:30.000
Who's having dinner with you?

00:23:30.030 --> 00:23:35.290
with Hoshi. Talk to her. See if he said anything about this. And go over the com logs. I want

00:23:35.290 --> 00:23:39.360
to know if he'd talk to anyone else. It might be a good idea to check his quotas as well.

00:23:42.650 --> 00:23:46.960
Post a security detail outside every section that's under repair. Nice, sir.

00:24:12.960 --> 00:24:17.370
- A member of my crew is dead.

00:24:17.370 --> 00:24:22.480
I don't know what happened.

00:24:22.480 --> 00:24:26.940
- Your inquiry was not recognized.

00:24:26.940 --> 00:24:30.000
- My helmsman killed

00:24:31.980 --> 00:24:40.240
launch bay one we think it happened while that section was off limits all

00:24:40.240 --> 00:24:45.110
personnel are required to vacate areas that are undergoing reconstruction we're

00:24:45.110 --> 00:24:54.930
aware of that you must have some kind of record of what happened all personnel

00:24:54.930 --> 00:24:58.420
are required to vacate areas that are undergoing reconstruction

00:25:00.990 --> 00:25:03.110
I need to talk to a person.

00:25:03.110 --> 00:25:10.310
Someone who can access your database and tell me what happened.

00:25:10.310 --> 00:25:12.690
Your inquiry was not recognized.

00:25:12.690 --> 00:25:15.720
Who built this station? What species?

00:25:15.720 --> 00:25:17.960
Your inquiry was not recognized.

00:25:17.960 --> 00:25:20.220
What species?

00:25:20.220 --> 00:25:29.000
Any damage to these facilities will be charged to your vessel.

00:25:31.790 --> 00:25:38.890
Subject's name, Ensign, Travis Mayweather, human male, weight, 72 kilograms, age 26.

00:25:38.890 --> 00:25:44.980
Earth years, are too young to be on this table.

00:25:44.980 --> 00:25:49.580
Cellular decay suggests that death occurred at approximately 23-30 hours.

00:25:49.580 --> 00:25:55.210
Preliminary cause of death, ventricular fibrillation induced by an isolytic shock.

00:25:55.210 --> 00:26:00.000
The vascular system appears to have functioned as a conduit, with a discharge, the musculature

00:26:00.000 --> 00:26:04.790
extensive necrosis along the conductive pathway there are subcutaneous burns

00:26:04.790 --> 00:26:11.900
over approximately 12% of the body the right phalanges and metacarpus exhibit

00:26:11.900 --> 00:26:20.100
signs of multiple thermal fractures computer pause ensign this is not an

00:26:20.100 --> 00:26:30.000
ideal time I wanted to say goodbye you may find this disturbing I've seen a

00:26:30.000 --> 00:26:33.940
a body before 15 of them on the alien ship it's different when it's someone

00:26:33.940 --> 00:26:57.880
you know personally hoping it was another one of his practical jokes

00:27:00.030 --> 00:27:04.430
- Travis called me down to Decon a few weeks ago,

00:27:04.430 --> 00:27:06.380
said that he brought some kind

00:27:06.380 --> 00:27:09.080
of gelatinous life form aboard.

00:27:09.080 --> 00:27:11.670
He said it might be sentient,

00:27:11.670 --> 00:27:14.580
that the captain needed me to figure out

00:27:14.580 --> 00:27:17.700
how to communicate with it.

00:27:17.700 --> 00:27:19.360
- I don't recall that.

00:27:19.360 --> 00:27:20.480
- There was no life form.

00:27:20.480 --> 00:27:25.660
It was only strawberry gelatin.

00:27:25.660 --> 00:27:27.240
Told him I was gonna get him back.

00:27:30.480 --> 00:27:34.290
- I'm sorry.

00:27:34.290 --> 00:27:37.430
- It might comfort you to know he felt very little pain.

00:27:37.430 --> 00:27:45.540
An isolytic shock instantly impairs the nervous...

00:27:45.540 --> 00:27:48.490
It's odd.

00:27:48.490 --> 00:27:51.970
- What?

00:27:51.970 --> 00:27:55.780
- Dead, all of them.

00:27:55.780 --> 00:27:57.430
Excuse me, Ensign.

00:28:11.840 --> 00:28:17.590
- Anything?

00:28:17.590 --> 00:28:21.650
- Travis used the comm system last night.

00:28:21.650 --> 00:28:23.610
Crewman Hayes says she passed him on his way

00:28:23.610 --> 00:28:25.270
to the launch bay.

00:28:25.270 --> 00:28:26.790
I didn't speak.

00:28:26.790 --> 00:28:28.450
She said he seemed to be in quite a hurry.

00:28:30.570 --> 00:28:31.320
- What's this?

00:28:31.320 --> 00:28:38.890
- The letter to his sister.

00:28:38.890 --> 00:28:42.530
It was on the monitor when it came in.

00:28:42.530 --> 00:28:50.450
I'm afraid there isn't much here.

00:28:50.450 --> 00:28:59.390
He mentioned something about canceling breakfast with him.

00:28:59.390 --> 00:29:00.000
- That was...

00:29:01.240 --> 00:29:07.490
Last week I had to postpone it.

00:29:07.490 --> 00:29:15.770
Have we been able to locate his parents?

00:29:15.770 --> 00:29:20.990
Sub-Commander DePaul's working on it, but it could take some time.

00:29:20.990 --> 00:29:23.080
Cargo ships aren't always easy to track down.

00:29:30.760 --> 00:29:32.030
- Verger.

00:29:32.030 --> 00:29:32.950
- It's Dr. Flops, Captain.

00:29:32.950 --> 00:29:42.840
I need to see you right away.

00:29:42.840 --> 00:29:44.620
Did you find something?

00:29:44.620 --> 00:29:46.160
- Matter of fact, I did.

00:29:46.160 --> 00:29:50.300
This is not Ensign Mayweather.

00:29:50.300 --> 00:29:51.250
- What?

00:29:51.250 --> 00:29:53.090
- It's a nearly perfect replica.

00:29:53.090 --> 00:29:54.590
I've never seen a life form duplicated

00:29:54.590 --> 00:29:55.970
in such extraordinary detail,

00:29:55.970 --> 00:29:59.380
from its epidermis down to its cellular proteins.

00:30:00.000 --> 00:30:02.340
- This is remarkable work.

00:30:02.340 --> 00:30:06.820
- If it's so perfect, how do you know it's not him?

00:30:06.820 --> 00:30:08.580
- Do you recall what happened to crewman Fisher

00:30:08.580 --> 00:30:12.500
last month after our visit to Tesic Prime?

00:30:12.500 --> 00:30:15.450
- He came down with red jelly and fear.

00:30:15.450 --> 00:30:17.730
- I inoculated the entire crew to prevent an outbreak.

00:30:17.730 --> 00:30:21.060
Would you mind rolling up your sleeve?

00:30:30.000 --> 00:30:32.980
The vaccine contained millions of genetically altered microbes.

00:30:32.980 --> 00:30:34.760
Most of them are still in your bloodstream.

00:30:34.760 --> 00:30:46.470
They typically survive for, oh, at least several weeks.

00:30:46.470 --> 00:30:51.260
Every one of the alien microbes in this body is dead.

00:30:51.260 --> 00:30:54.040
Couldn't they have been killed by the isolitic shock?

00:30:54.040 --> 00:30:55.940
The microbes thrive on isolitic energy.

00:30:55.940 --> 00:30:57.950
If anything, they would have multiplied.

00:30:57.950 --> 00:31:00.000
I believe that someone or something

00:31:00.830 --> 00:31:07.640
have subducted ensign mayweather and left this uh facsimile in his place apparently

00:31:07.640 --> 00:31:12.950
bulkheads aren't the only thing this station can replicate it's ironic in a way the station

00:31:12.950 --> 00:31:17.390
can duplicate a dead human body in all its exquisite detail yet a living simple one-celled

00:31:17.390 --> 00:31:26.160
organism is beyond its capability i've located ensign mayweather's parents better hold off

00:31:26.160 --> 00:31:30.000
their son may still be alive you and trip managed to get pretty

00:31:30.000 --> 00:31:34.410
far inside the station. How close do you think you got to the computer core? We were within

00:31:34.410 --> 00:31:40.010
20 meters when we tripped the sensors. Think you could find a way to get past them? I believe

00:31:40.010 --> 00:31:46.690
so. Our repairs will be complete in 19 minutes. The station's expecting us to depart. Bridge

00:31:46.690 --> 00:31:52.050
to engineering. Tucker here. Tripp, have you prepared our payment? The canisters are almost

00:31:52.050 --> 00:31:58.100
ready, sir. Don't be in such a hurry.

00:32:07.960 --> 00:32:11.400
200 liters of warp plasma, as promised.

00:32:11.400 --> 00:32:13.120
- Please place your compensation

00:32:13.120 --> 00:32:18.140
on the transport platform.

00:32:18.140 --> 00:32:20.160
- Hold on, hold on.

00:32:20.160 --> 00:32:23.870
There's a couple of problems we need to discuss first.

00:32:23.870 --> 00:32:28.610
I'm not real happy with the quality of some of your work.

00:32:28.610 --> 00:32:29.700
You listening to me?

00:32:30.000 --> 00:32:33.480
Please place your compensation on the transport platform.

00:32:33.480 --> 00:32:37.340
I've looked at the bolt couplings you used to attach a new hull plating.

00:32:37.340 --> 00:32:41.120
I'm afraid they're not up to Starfleet specs.

00:32:41.120 --> 00:32:43.400
And the subspace amplifier you repaired?

00:32:43.400 --> 00:32:47.630
We're picking up distortion on all the high band frequencies.

00:32:47.630 --> 00:32:51.320
Please place your compensation on the transport platform.

00:32:51.320 --> 00:32:55.700
We're not paying until we sort this out.

00:33:07.610 --> 00:33:15.900
I have that these duranium pins won't fly out the instant we jump to warp your inquiry was not recognized

00:33:17.210 --> 00:33:28.100
On my world we have an expression customers always right. Maybe you should make that part of your program

00:33:32.460 --> 00:33:36.080
I want to know how someone files a grievance around here.

00:34:30.000 --> 00:34:35.890
like you've got things to deal with

00:35:51.020 --> 00:35:56.630
"Precursion detected in primary data core. Vacate the section or your vessel will be compromised."

00:35:56.630 --> 00:35:58.390
"Detected one human biosign."

00:36:00.000 --> 00:36:03.150
Are they alive?

00:36:03.150 --> 00:36:05.990
Your vital organs appear to be functioning.

00:36:05.990 --> 00:36:08.390
They've suffered severe neurological damage.

00:36:08.390 --> 00:36:11.460
Incursion detected in primary data core.

00:36:11.460 --> 00:36:15.910
Vacate this section or your vessel will be compromised.

00:36:15.910 --> 00:36:18.640
Their synaptic pathways have been reconfigured,

00:36:18.640 --> 00:36:23.100
integrated into the computer core.

00:36:23.100 --> 00:36:26.160
Incursion detected in primary data core.

00:36:26.160 --> 00:36:29.700
Vacate this section or your vessel will be compromised.

00:36:30.800 --> 00:36:31.570
"Captain."

00:36:31.570 --> 00:36:44.050
"Persia detected in primary data core. Vacate the section or your vessel will be compromised."

00:37:00.480 --> 00:37:02.630
The three of the station's arms have just clamped onto the hull.

00:37:02.630 --> 00:37:03.730
Polarize the hull plating.

00:37:04.500 --> 00:37:05.430
There's no effect.

00:37:05.430 --> 00:37:06.430
Standby weapons.

00:37:06.430 --> 00:37:10.110
They're going offline.

00:37:10.110 --> 00:37:13.630
The station's tapped into the ship's umbilical ports.

00:37:13.630 --> 00:37:16.990
It's overriding our command functions.

00:37:16.990 --> 00:37:18.530
Try to lock out the main computer.

00:37:18.530 --> 00:37:22.380
I can't. Our access code's been scrambled.

00:37:22.380 --> 00:37:25.560
It's okay, Travis. We're taking you home.

00:37:25.560 --> 00:37:27.520
Right here.

00:38:02.300 --> 00:38:03.040
Archer to the ridge.

00:38:03.200 --> 00:38:03.820
It calms down.

00:38:08.920 --> 00:38:09.220
Travis?

00:38:09.510 --> 00:38:10.270
On his way to stick pay.

00:38:10.330 --> 00:38:10.970
What's our status?

00:38:11.110 --> 00:38:11.590
It's been better.

00:38:12.070 --> 00:38:13.350
The station's got us by the thrusters.

00:38:13.800 --> 00:38:14.540
Impulse engines?

00:38:16.140 --> 00:38:18.320
Offline.

00:38:19.750 --> 00:38:20.570
We're losing main power.

00:38:21.090 --> 00:38:21.990
Life support's failing.

00:38:22.510 --> 00:38:22.790
Malcolm?

00:38:23.290 --> 00:38:25.150
It's time we deliver our payment.

00:38:43.020 --> 00:38:48.610
some heavy damage sir. Power levels are dropping, but the plasma hasn't ignited the O2 conduits

00:38:48.610 --> 00:38:53.300
yet. It needs to reach 3,000 degrees Malcolm, be patient. Yes sir.

00:39:02.840 --> 00:39:14.090
reading secondary explosions throughout the station functions are coming back

00:39:14.090 --> 00:39:19.080
online engines impulse and thrusters one of those arms is still locked onto the

00:39:19.080 --> 00:39:29.760
hole don't disengage soon we'll be incinerated all thrusters

00:39:30.000 --> 00:39:33.720
No good, and if I fired up the impulse engines, we'd probably tear off half the saucer section.

00:39:33.720 --> 00:39:35.310
Can you launch a torpedo?

00:39:35.310 --> 00:39:37.580
In this range, sir, I wouldn't recommend it.

00:39:37.580 --> 00:39:39.800
I agree, but I don't think we have much choice.

00:39:39.800 --> 00:39:51.060
One more, Lieutenant.

00:40:00.640 --> 00:40:01.240
Get us out of here.

00:40:15.160 --> 00:40:25.700
You look pretty good for a dead guy.

00:40:28.360 --> 00:40:28.820
How are you feeling?

00:40:31.310 --> 00:40:42.820
much better sir thank you the doctor told me what happened i'm not sure i understand we're still

00:40:42.820 --> 00:40:51.480
trying to figure that out for ourselves i may be able to shed some light on the subject it seems

00:40:51.480 --> 00:40:55.890
to be some kind of interface designed to convert neural impulses into binary code

00:40:55.890 --> 00:41:00.000
essentially the station was using your brain to enhance its

00:41:00.030 --> 00:41:06.700
Processing power. Why would it do that? The cerebral cortex is the most sophisticated computer known to exist

00:41:07.280 --> 00:41:18.140
Those other people according to Paul scans most of them have been there for years the damage to their brains was irreversible

00:41:19.960 --> 00:41:25.430
Fortunately, you were removed before any permanent injury occurred. When can I have my helmsman back?

00:41:25.610 --> 00:41:30.000
I'd like to observe him for another 24 hours if you don't mind

00:41:37.840 --> 00:41:42.400
Captain's Mess. Friday morning, 0800. Don't be late.

00:41:43.660 --> 00:41:44.620
Sounds good, sir.
